# Terminus Core Standards

Project Terminus benchmarks AI coding agents on real Docker-container engineering tasks.

## Difficulty (benchmark: GPT-5.5 + Claude Opus 4.8)

- Hard: ≤20% on best or worst model
- Medium: 20–60% on worst model
- Easy: 60–80% on worst model
- **Rejected if >80%** on worst model
- **New submissions:** easy tier blocked; Python tasks must be hard

## Category & Subtypes

- `category`: one of 9 types — see `docs/task-type-taxonomy.md`
- `subcategories`: long_context, tool_specific, api_integration, db_interaction, ui_building
- Milestone tasks preferred for new submissions — see `docs/guidelines/milestones.md`

## Non-Negotiables

- `allow_internet = false` in task.toml `[environment]`
- All test deps pre-installed in Dockerfile; test.sh must NOT install packages
- Digest-pin every `FROM` with `@sha256:<digest>`
- Install tmux + asciinema in Dockerfile
- Never COPY solution/ or tests/ into image
- No solution hints/walkthroughs in environment files
- No AI scaffolding filenames (CLAUDE.md, skills.md, AGENTS.md)

## Workflow

1. `stb init` → develop → `./scripts/terminus validate` → oracle → agent test → zip → submit
2. Rubric via platform UI (not CLI); ≥3 negative rewards
3. Run `./scripts/terminus check-all <task-dir>` before every submission

